[h1]All-in-one stats for Slay the Spire 2, made for co-op[/h1]
Damage, protection, debuffs, help between players, missed opportunities, trophies and records.
Read-only: it never changes the game. Works in solo and in multiplayer, [b]even when your friends don't have it[/b] (only one player needs it: every player's game simulates the whole fight).

[b]{BRANCH_EN}[/b]

[h2]What it shows[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]The panel[/b] (F7): one line per player, tabs [i]last turn[/i], [i]combat[/i] and [i]run[/i]. Damage by source, damage actually stopped by block, debuffs, missed opportunities (missed lethal, wasted block, weaker choices, unused energy...), co-op help (block given, HP saved, energy and cards given, friendly fire), campfires, cards and potions.
[*][b]Combat summary:[/b] a round-by-round chart of every fight of the run.
[*][b]Trophies:[/b] the best player in each category, all-time records, personal bests, records per character.
[*][b]Group compositions[/b] (F8): how often each group of characters was played and won, per ascension.
[*][b]Settings[/b] (gear button): English / Français, sections and columns, separate windows, hotkeys.
[/list]
Every number follows a written rule: [url=https://github.com/Zaille75/KikiMAIster/blob/main/docs/specs/01-metrics.md]the rules[/url].

[h2]Bugs and ideas[/h2]
Press [b]F9[/b] in game: the mod makes a zip (screenshot, game state, log, with names and Steam ids removed) and opens a GitHub issue page: drop the zip on it. Source code and changelog: [url=https://github.com/Zaille75/KikiMAIster]github.com/Zaille75/KikiMAIster[/url] (MIT).

Your settings, records and run files are kept in the game's user folder (%APPDATA%\SlayTheSpire2\KikiMAIster), so updates never erase them.

[h1]Français[/h1]
Toutes les stats de Slay the Spire 2, pensées pour la coop : dégâts, protection, affaiblissements, entraide, occasions manquées, trophées et records. Le mod ne change rien au jeu. Il marche en solo et en multi, [b]même si tes amis ne l'ont pas[/b].

[b]{BRANCH_FR}[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Le panneau[/b] (F7) : une ligne par joueur, onglets [i]tour précédent[/i], [i]combat[/i] et [i]partie[/i].
[*][b]Résumé du combat[/b], [b]Trophées[/b] et records, [b]Compositions de groupe[/b] (F8).
[*][b]Paramètres[/b] : English / Français, sections, colonnes, fenêtres à part, touches.
[*][b]F9[/b] : signaler un bug ou une idée (zip + page GitHub).
[/list]
